{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_020 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat, multiprofile) achieved only 50.7% accuracy at 3.95 GPU hours — the most expensive setup in the space. With just one data point, the critical uncertainty is whether the large image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) is actually contributing meaningful signal or is simply adding cost without accuracy benefit. Question tested: config_006 is a clean single-variable change from config_020 (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50), isolating the image-encoder choice while holding RNA encoder (scgpt), aggregation (transformer), fusion (concat), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly answers whether the dominant cost driver (vit_l) is worth its compute, which will shape all remaining 8 experiments; (2) if resnet50 matches or approaches 50.7%, every subsequent experiment becomes substantially cheaper, freeing budget for more informative searches; (3) if resnet50 is clearly worse, we confirm vit_l is essential and can focus remaining budget on other dimensions (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion). Expected relative cost: moderate — roughly 2.5–3.0 GPU hours, about 25–35% cheaper than config_020, since resnet50 is significantly lighter than ViT-L while transformer aggregation and scgpt remain."
}

